# fp64 without fp64: a double computation over f32, with f32 alone or as
# double-word pairs (hi + lo of two f32, built on the error-free 2Sum,
# Fast2Sum and 2Prod), when the active cost model prices that below its
# f64 operations and the derived error bound meets what the result needs.
# gt1030 (f64 at 1/32 rate) takes the pairs; an x86 model (f64 as cheap as
# f32) takes nothing.
#
# a difference of squares in double, the result an f32
dsq(x: f32 in 1..2, y: f32 in 3..4) = f32(f64(x) * f64(x) - f64(y) * f64(y))
cost dsq
dword dsq
# the form is a function: priced, and measured against the double version
cost dsq_dw
error dsq_dw ~ dsq
# the same request under a model with cheap f64: no candidate is cheaper
dword dsq model zen4
# a looser requirement: f32 alone meets 4 ulp, and is cheaper still
dword dsq ulp 4
# overlapping ranges: x*x - y*y can cancel, so there is no relative
# bound; an absolute tolerance is met
can(x: f32 in 1..2, y: f32 in 1..2) = f32(f64(x) * f64(x) - f64(y) * f64(y))
dword can
dword can atol 1e-12
# a product less a float, which may cancel too: DWPlusFP's bound holds
# whatever cancels (by cases on the high words), so it is relative
cxf(a: f32 in 1..2, b: f32 in 1..2, c: f32 in 1..4) = f32(f64(a) * f64(b) - f64(c))
dword cxf
# division and square root
hyp(a: f32 in 1..100, b: f32 in 1..100) = f32(f64(a) / sqrt(f64(a) * f64(a) + f64(b) * f64(b)))
dword hyp
# an f64 result needs a tolerance; the pair is recombined
acc(x: f32 in 0.5..2, y: f32 in 0.5..2) = f64(x) * f64(y) / (f64(x) + f64(y))
dword acc
dword acc tol 1e-12
# the prices decide: one f64 multiply-add, which the model fuses, costs
# less than its pair and the recombination
one(x: f32 in 0.5..2, y: f32 in 0.5..2) = f64(x) * f64(y) + f64(x)
dword one tol 1e-12
# an f64 parameter is split in place, a constant when it is read
sc(t: f64 in 0.1..10, x: f32 in 1..2) = f32((t * f64(x) + 0.1) / (t + f64(x)))
dword sc
# integers: up to 24 bits convert exactly, a u32 in two exact parts
iu(i: u32, x: f32 in 1..2) = f32(f64(i) * f64(x))
dword iu
# what has no pair form stays in f64 and is split
tr(x: f32 in 0.1..1) = f32(sin(f64(x)) * f64(x))
dword tr
# no ranges: the bound holds under conditions the caller keeps
nr(x: f32, y: f32) = f32(f64(x) * f64(y) * f64(x))
dword nr
# English
avoid fp64 in tr
dsq without doubles, within 4 ulp
emulate doubles in hyp on zen4
# find says so
find dsq
# a conversion round trip the driver folds: gt1030 declares f32 -> f16 ->
# f32 (measured: dropped), so it costs nothing there and does not round
q(x: f32 in 0.5..8) = f32(f16(x)) * 2
cost q
foldproof q
cost q_fp
# every f32: subnormal results, overflow to infinity, NaN
qa(x: f32) = f32(f16(x))
foldproof qa
# an integer of 11 bits is an f16 value: nothing is lost
qi(i: u8) = f32(f16(f32(i))) + 1
cost qi
foldproof qi
# a model that folds nothing computes the round trip as written
cost q model zen4
foldproof q model zen4
# a model can declare the fold
model mine : zen4 { folds f32 -> f16 -> f32 }
cost q model mine
# English
make qi fold-proof
does the driver fold q under zen4
